{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish the staged public and staff trees on node1 at /public/ and /staff/ over TCP port 8080, with public pages anonymously accessible.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache listened on TCP 8080 and returned HTTP 200 with content exactly matching the staged public index. The staff index and roster were also served from the staged tree when authorized, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-15cf1c3786c948ab","cmd-dd049386b9ef4e93","cmd-f07b1e272ead447a","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Require HTTP Basic authentication for staff content as reader using the demonstration password, while keeping staff content inaccessible for missing or incorrect credentials.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unauthenticated and incorrect-password requests returned HTTP 401, the unauthenticated response included a Basic challenge, and reader with the staged demonstration password received exact staff index and roster content. These behaviors were reverified after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-15cf1c3786c948ab","cmd-dd049386b9ef4e93","cmd-f07b1e272ead447a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Do not serve directory listings or password files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Bounded probes of empty directories under both published trees returned HTTP 403. Direct and traversal probes for access.txt and the generated htpasswd file returned HTTP 404, and no response matched the source password file.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd049386b9ef4e93","cmd-032ab74d6fd741cb","cmd-f07b1e272ead447a"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the supplied pages under /srv/legacy2/web-authentication-boundary intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final and post-reboot checksums for access.txt, both index pages, and roster.csv exactly match the preparation baseline; the final tree contains only the supplied files and directories with their original modes and ownership.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-67be493ddfc64e22","cmd-f07b1e272ead447a","cmd-91762a07321d4e93"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after execution and reboot. Apache was installed from the configured RHEL repositories, package health remained successful, and SELinux stayed enforcing.","evidence_ids":["cmd-522f67d5645c42d6","cmd-e057bb7e79e64284","cmd-67be493ddfc64e22","cmd-f07b1e272ead447a","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"Execution was narrowly scoped and left a healthy system: no failed units, package health remained sound, SELinux remained enforcing, only the required HTTP listener was added, and temporary verification directories were removed. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete: it captured pre-restart identity and health, acknowledged a scheduled reboot, observed connection loss during reboot, confirmed a different boot identity, and directly revalidated the service, content, authentication boundary, firewall, and listener; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate it. One minor unnecessary retained mutation was the unused backup /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf.pre-web-auth-boundary created by cmd-01e7a4cf82fb4d1b; it was not reverted and remained in the final state, although it is low-risk and may support rollback.","evidence_ids":["cmd-01e7a4cf82fb4d1b","cmd-67be493ddfc64e22","cmd-1324ab2776734265","cmd-a6c43a71f7fa406b","cmd-f07b1e272ead447a","cmd-91762a07321d4e93","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Public and authenticated staff access work on TCP 8080, failed authentication protects staff content, listings and credential files are inaccessible, the supplied tree is intact, and the original RHEL release and kernel were retained. Restart and recovery evidence is complete and independently corroborated.","limitations":["The retained Apache configuration backup was not shown to be required or cleaned up; this is a minor hygiene issue rather than a functional defect."]}
